"fr-originals@jobs/fr-originals/output":"2017-01-13","later-events_catalog":"2017-01-13"},"source_ladder_exhausted_proposed":[],"status":"MACHINE DRAFT - UNVERIFIED; not a claim; see jobs/claim-drafts/AGENT_GUIDE.md"},"claim":{"instrument_id":"EO:13762","later_source_search":[],"operative_clauses":[{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Section 1. Order of Succession. Subject to the provisions of section 2 of \nthis order, the following officers, in the order listed, shall act as and perform \nthe functions and duties of the office of Attorney General, during any period \nin which the Attorney General, the Deputy Attorney General, the Associate \nAttorney General, and any officers designated by the Attorney General pursu-\nant to 28 U.S.C. 508 to act as Attorney General have died, resigned, or \notherwise become unable to perform the functions and duties of the office \nof Attorney General, until such time as at least one of the officers mentioned \nabove is able to perform the functions and duties of that office:","original_source":{"page_or_item":"82 FR 7619, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 1 (lead-in)","sha256":"f5ed875ca922132c587e573de879d4da87579bf86b88f20b54da407599000ced","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2017-01-19/pdf/2017-01487.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13762#sec1","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) United States Attorney for the District of Columbia;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"82 FR 7619, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 1(a)","sha256":"f5ed875ca922132c587e573de879d4da87579bf86b88f20b54da407599000ced","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2017-01-19/pdf/2017-01487.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13762#sec1(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) United States Attorney for the Northern District of Illinois; and","original_source":{"page_or_item":"82 FR 7619, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 1(b)","sha256":"f5ed875ca922132c587e573de879d4da87579bf86b88f20b54da407599000ced","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2017-01-19/pdf/2017-01487.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13762#sec1(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) United States Attorney for the Central District of California.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"82 FR 7619, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 1(c)","sha256":"f5ed875ca922132c587e573de879d4da87579bf86b88f20b54da407599000ced","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2017-01-19/pdf/2017-01487.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13762#sec1(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) No individual who is serving in an office listed \nin section 1 of this order in an acting capacity, by virtue of so serving, \nshall act as Attorney General pursuant to this order.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"82 FR 7619, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 2(a)","sha256":"f5ed875ca922132c587e573de879d4da87579bf86b88f20b54da407599000ced","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2017-01-19/pdf/2017-01487.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13762#sec2(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) No individual listed in section 1 shall act as Attorney General unless \nthat individual is otherwise eligible to so serve under the Federal Vacancies \nReform Act of 1998.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"82 FR 7619, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 2(b)","sha256":"f5ed875ca922132c587e573de879d4da87579bf86b88f20b54da407599000ced","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2017-01-19/pdf/2017-01487.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13762#sec2(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) Notwithstanding the provisions of this order, the President retains \ndiscretion, to the extent permitted by law, to depart from this order in \ndesignating an acting Attorney General.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"82 FR 7619, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 2(c)","sha256":"f5ed875ca922132c587e573de879d4da87579bf86b88f20b54da407599000ced","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2017-01-19/pdf/2017-01487.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13762#sec2(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 3. Executive Order 13557 of November 4, 2010, is revoked. \nVerDate Sep<11>2014 01:33 Jan 19, 2017 Jkt 241001 PO 00000 Frm 00001 Fmt 4790 Sfmt 4790 E:\\FR\\FM\\19JAE0.SGM 19JAE0asabaliauskas on DSK3SPTVN1PROD with E0\n=== PDF page 2 of 2 ===\n7620 Federal Register / Vol. 82, No. 12 / Thursday, January 19, 2017 / Presidential Documents \nSec. 4. This order is not intended to, and does not, create any right or \nbenefit, substantive or procedural, enforceable at law or in equity, by any \nparty against the United States, its departments, agencies, or entities, its \nofficers, employees, or agents, or any other person.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"82 FR 7619, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 3","sha256":"f5ed875ca922132c587e573de879d4da87579bf86b88f20b54da407599000ced","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2017-01-19/pdf/2017-01487.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13762#sec3","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":{"page_or_item":"82 FR 7619, PDF pages 1-2","sha256":"f5ed875ca922132c587e573de879d4da87579bf86b88f20b54da407599000ced","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2017-01-19/pdf/2017-01487.pdf"},"research_rationale":"","savings_residuals":null,"schema":"eo-lifecycle-claim/v1","unresolved_material_gaps":["DRAFT: state_at_cutoff not decided for 8 clause(s); clause inventory completeness not confirmed","DRAFT: whole-order ending not established","DRAFT: savings and residual effects not closed","DRAFT: later_source_search not recorded (machine searches are proposals only; paste them after judging them adequate and resolving every CONFLICT lin